WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:05.038
-The "Community" cast
had a virtual reunion.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:06.506
-Yes.

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.173
-How did it go? Was it fun?

00:00:08.173 --> 00:00:10.242
Did you enjoy doing that?

00:00:10.242 --> 00:00:13.546
-Oh, it was -- I can't --
I mean, now I'm being sincere,

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:17.150
but it was -- it was like
going to a family reunion

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:19.452
with family that
you actually liked.

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:22.955
-Aww.
-And it was -- I cried after.

00:00:22.955 --> 00:00:25.257
Like, we all were
texting afterwards,

00:00:25.257 --> 00:00:27.227
and we were all so happy.

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:29.595
Yeah, we raised a bunch of money
for Frontline Foods

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:32.765
for essential workers and for
the World Central Kitchen.

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:36.503
And, you know, like -- you know,
Donald Glover was there,

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:38.972
and he's -- as you know,
his career has tanked.

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.974
So this is --
He really needed this.

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:46.679
-He needed the virtual
"Community" reunion.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:48.247
-You know,
the "Star Wars" movies

00:00:48.247 --> 00:00:51.518
and the Emmys and the Grammys.
-Yeah, sure. Of course.

00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:55.321
-Like, none of those have really
helped his career, so this --

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.423
-You've all done pretty well.

00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:59.692
What is the -- There's a rumor

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.861
that a possibility of
a "Community" movie.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:04.864
-Yes, and we are coming to you

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:08.868
to ask
for some financing because

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:14.274
we know you have that -- I think
NBC calls it "F-You" money,

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:16.075
which I think is an insult.

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:20.346
No, there is a g--
there's a good chance, I think,

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:24.049
because on the Zoom,
everyone got asked,

00:01:24.049 --> 00:01:26.953
and Donald said he would do it.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:29.421
And he's the busiest man
in show business, so --

00:01:29.421 --> 00:01:31.757
and then Dan -- we'll see
because Dan's got to write it,

00:01:31.757 --> 00:01:34.961
and he's got like
100 "Rick and Morty" episodes

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.395
that he has to make.
-Yeah.

00:01:36.395 --> 00:01:39.566
-But I think we would all do it
if we are --

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:43.202
you know, if we're --
If Dan writes it,

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:45.939
it sounds like people will make
themselves available.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:47.907
-That would be a lot of fun.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:50.343
You're hosting the second season
of "Card Sharks."

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:51.844
You were here
for the first season,

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:55.715
and it went on to be
the biggest summer show of ABC

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:58.017
in like 10 years or something
crazy like that.

00:01:58.017 --> 00:01:59.418
Congratulations on that.

00:01:59.418 --> 00:02:01.054
You're one of the first shows
to go back

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:02.855
into production
during the pandemic.

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:04.290
What was that like?
-Yeah.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:07.160
Well, it's nice of you
to say the show was popular.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:11.530
No, it -- we --
Us and "The Mandalorian"

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.299
were the first shows
back in production,

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:18.071
and as you know,
both shows are equally popular

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:23.109
and same audience
and production value.

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:25.645
But see, the thing is
we're better than "Mandalorian"

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:28.448
because we gave away money,
and what did they give us?

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:31.384
Just a wonderful, adorable,
you know, baby Yoda.

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:33.686
That's -- That's not cash money.

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:38.090
So, yeah -- no, I -- I --
Thankfully it worked,

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:42.995
and they had all these zones
that people moved in.

00:02:42.995 --> 00:02:46.399
There was -- At one point, they
thought somebody was positive,

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.201
but it was just
an inconclusive test,

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.968
but those people
were quarantined.

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:51.337
We were able to continue.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.106
-Yeah, you got to
take it seriously. Yeah.

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:56.242
-Yeah. So actually --
it actually worked.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:03:00.480
And as you know, there's so many
people not working right now,

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:04.783
so to have a way to proceed
and have people get to be able

00:03:04.783 --> 00:03:06.885
to make money for their families
has been --

00:03:06.885 --> 00:03:08.754
you know, it's great.

00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:13.025
So I -- You know, what I'm
saying is I'm responsible for...

00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:14.359
-[ Laughs ] Just stop.

00:03:14.359 --> 00:03:16.729
-...the recovery of
the economy, so you're welcome.

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.331
You're welcome. Cheers.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:20.800
That's not what
you're saying at all.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.734
-I don't know
how to end sentences!

00:03:22.734 --> 00:03:23.870
It just kind of ramps up,

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.571
and I just keep going,
and I can't stop.

00:03:25.571 --> 00:03:27.306
I don't know.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:28.641
You're a funny guy.

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.309
You're a loving guy.

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:32.645
You give back whenever you can,
and I appreciate that.

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:34.080
You know I'm a big fan.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.481
Congrats on the new season.

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:38.217
Have a great fall season.
Stay safe, please.

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:40.620
-Thank you.
-And save a bottle of wine

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.388
for when we can hang out
with each other, okay?

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:44.356
-I've got -- And just send me
your -- Just tell me

00:03:44.356 --> 00:03:45.425
your address of your house

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:47.059
that you invited me to
during the break.

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:48.795
That would be great.
Just go ahead.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:54.199
-The new season of "Card Sharks"
premieres October 18th on ABC.

00:03:54.199 --> 00:03:56.068
We're talking to Big Sean
when we come back.

00:03:56.068 --> 00:03:57.503
Stick around, everybody.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:00.839
-I'm dropping an album too.
It's called "Detroit 2," so...

00:04:00.839 --> 00:04:03.209
-Like, "also," T-O-O?

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:06.345
-Oh, no, I can't believe it.
It's the same name. Shoot.

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:08.548
Well, tell Sean I had it first,
and he has to change it.

